<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhojeshwar Temple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Bhojpur Shiva temple</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bhojeshwar Temple at Bhojpur, near Bhopal in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, is an unfinished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiva">Shiva</a> temple attributed to the Paramara king Bhoja in the 11th century. It houses one of the largest stone lingams in India, about 7.5 metres high including its platform, and the abandoned earthen ramp and plans engraved on nearby rocks show how such temples were built.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bhojeshwar-temple.jpg" alt="Bhojeshwar Temple" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shiva_Temple,_Bhojpur_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
